static ORION_STUDIO_SC_PARAM_25_READBACK: ParamReference = ParamReference { text: "frame.readback category 0x1a -- 16 records (one per speaker), 116 bytes each = a 4-byte header (`00 00 58 02`) then the 16 EQ bands in the EXACT `<freq LE16><Q LE16 x100><gain LE16 signed><mode>` layout of this write frame's [23_onward]. LIVE-CONFIRMED 2026-09-04: with a 2.0 Room Correction curve loaded, cat 0x1a idx 0 and idx 1 both carried that curve (identical L/R, as RC does), other indices were flat defaults. So this frame IS readable -- only the delay/level/invert head of the strip is not visible in cat 0x1a (bands only). Parsed + wired 2026-09-04: protocol.parse_surround_speaker_eq_record, CLI `surround-eq`. (The GLOBAL 0xab frame's readback is a separate category, 0x1b -- see params.surround_monitor.)", formula: "", offsets: &[] };
